# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lecture 41 vignette pool B -- sarcoidosis (presentation, confirmation, radiographic stage I-IV worked from the
described film, steroid indications and what to use instead, follow-up), coal workers' pneumoconiosis,
asbestosis and mesothelioma, and silicosis (slides 39-64).

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.
EXPLANATIONS follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md.

Held for the scope's slide conflicts: corticosteroids appear in NO coal workers' pneumoconiosis or silicosis item
(s54 line keyed for neither disease); the angiotensin-converting enzyme appears in NO silicosis item (s25); the
onset speed of silicosis is never asked (s60 against s61); the s41 sarcoid pathophysiology is never keyed; the
upper-lung reason (lighter dust) is used for silica only. Erythema nodosum and lupus pernio carry their s43
picture descriptions in the stem (NAMED), and so does eggshell calcification (hilar) and ferruginous bodies (dust).
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
